                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "In performing a physical assessment of a client with chronic kidney disease (CKD), which finding would the nurse anticipate?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nCKD is a condition in which the kidneys have progressive problems in clearing nitrogenous waste products and controlling fluid and electrolyte balance within the body. Cardiovascular symptoms of heart failure and hypertension are caused by the fluid volume overload resulting from the kidneys' inability to excrete water. Signs and symptoms of heart failure include jugular venous distention, S3 heart sound, pedal edema, increased weight, shortness of breath, and crackles auscultated in the lungs. The typical signs and symptoms of CKD include proteinuria or hematuria, not glycosuria. The nurse would observe anorexia and nausea in this client, not polyphagia.",
                        "id": "16cd620bc4854f85aff2a77e2a854835",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "cbc6270da4644c9995a5f20e9943cd7c",
                                "content": "Peritonitis"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "75412e1356c14ca6bff40e4f0c34ab92",
                                "content": "Hyperglycemia"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "00c74a0769314bf99be89fc931d55765",
                                "content": "Hyperphosphatemia"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "3ad26d4a8b4f4aa39df31593413c931e",
                                "content": "Disequilibrium syndrome"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "cbc6270da4644c9995a5f20e9943cd7c",
                                    "content": "Peritonitis"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "1",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "75412e1356c14ca6bff40e4f0c34ab92",
                                    "content": "Hyperglycemia"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "00c74a0769314bf99be89fc931d55765",
                                    "content": "Hyperphosphatemia"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "3ad26d4a8b4f4aa39df31593413c931e",
                                    "content": "Disequilibrium syndrome"
